{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) is requesting implementation of task #5157: extending `cmd/tee` to fully implement srd017-tee requirements R1.5, R2.1, R2.2, and R2.3. Specifically:\n   - **R1.5**: Must write output in the order received from stdin (buffering permitted but no reordering)\n   - **R2.1**: `-a` or `--append` must open each output file in append mode (O_APPEND)\n   - **R2.2**: `-i` or `--ignore-interrupts` must cause tee to ignore SIGINT signal\n   - **R2.3**: `-a` and `-i` may be combined; their effects are independent\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/tee/main.go` and `cmd/tee/tee_test.go`. Must not use git commands. Must pass AC1-AC4 acceptance criteria.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go Unix utility reimplementation matching GNU coreutils behavior\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` against Homebrew `gtee`\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - SIGINT signal suppression using Go's `os/signal` package\n   - `io.MultiWriter` for simultaneous multi-destination I/O\n   - `O_APPEND` file flag for append mode\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gtee\")` with `t.Skip` for graceful test skipping\n   - The `DiffTest` struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd017-tee.yaml`**\n     - Full SRD defining all tee requirements R1-R4\n     - Critical for understanding what R1.5, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 require\n     - Non-goals: no `--output-error` modes, no `-p` flag, no FIFO special semantics\n   \n   - **`cmd/tee/main.go`** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Already implements basic tee: stdin→stdout + files, `-a` append, file creation/truncation\n     - `-i` flag is parsed but NOT implemented (line 53-54: `case 'i': // R2.2: accepted, full implementation in future task`)\n     - `parseFlags` returns `(bool, []string)` — only appendMode and files, NOT ignoreInterrupts\n     - `openFile` already handles O_APPEND correctly\n     - `copyStdin` uses `io.MultiWriter` which preserves order (R1.5)\n     - Does NOT handle `--append` or `--ignore-interrupts` long flags\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         appendMode, files := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n         writers, closers, exitCode := openOutputs(files, appendMode)\n         defer closeAll(closers)\n         if err := copyStdin(writers); err != nil {\n             if !errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tee: %v\\n\", err)\n                 exitCode = 1\n             }\n         }\n         if exitCode != 0 { os.Exit(exitCode) }\n     }\n     \n     func parseFlags(args []string) (bool, []string) {\n         appendMode := false\n         var files []string\n         endOfFlags := false\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             if endOfFlags || arg == \"\" || arg[0] != '-' {\n                 files = append(files, arg)\n                 continue\n             }\n             if arg == \"--\" { endOfFlags = true; continue }\n             for _, c := range arg[1:] {\n                 switch c {\n                 case 'a': appendMode = true\n                 case 'i': // R2.2: accepted, full implementation in future task\n                 default:\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tee: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", c)\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n             }\n         }\n         return appendMode, files\n     }\n     ```\n   \n   - **`cmd/tee/tee_test.go`** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Has tests: TestDiff (passthrough), TestDiffSingleFile, TestDiffMultipleFiles, TestDiffDashFile, TestDiffAppendMode, TestFileCreation, TestTruncateExisting\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gtee\")`\n     - Helper functions: `runFileTest`, `runMultiFileTest`, `runAppendTest`, `allBytes`\n     - Missing tests for: R1.5 order verification, R2.2 SIGINT suppression, R2.3 combined flags, multi-file differential tests, `--append`/`--ignore-interrupts` long flags\n\n   - **`pkg/testutils/difftest.go`** (referenced, not modified)\n     - `DiffTest` struct with `Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles` fields\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` function\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for compilation\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — was still in the reading/planning phase.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R1.5 is already satisfied by `io.MultiWriter` (preserves write order)\n   - Identified that R2.1 (`-a` short flag) is already implemented in `openFile`, but `--append` long flag is missing\n   - Identified that R2.2 is the main implementation gap — `-i` is parsed but does nothing\n   - Determined the changes needed:\n     1. Modify `parseFlags` to return `ignoreInterrupts bool` and handle `--append`/`--ignore-interrupts` long flags\n     2. Add `signal.Ignore(os.Interrupt)` in `main()` when ignoreInterrupts is true\n     3. Add differential test cases for R1.5, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive task prompt containing: role description, repository files list, project context (VISION, ARCHITECTURE, SPECIFICATIONS, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, execution constitution, go style constitution, shared protocols, package contracts, and constraints.\n   - The task message specifies task #5157: `[stitch] cmd/tee: multi-file output, append mode, and SIGINT suppression (srd017-tee R1.5, R2.1-R2.3)`\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/tee/main.go` to:\n     - Make `parseFlags` return `ignoreInterrupts` boolean\n     - Handle `--append` and `--ignore-interrupts` long flags in parseFlags\n     - Add SIGINT suppression logic in `main()` using `signal.Ignore(os.Interrupt)` when `-i` is set\n   - Modify `cmd/tee/tee_test.go` to:\n     - Add differential test cases for R1.5 (write ordering)\n     - Add differential test cases for R2.1 (append mode with `--append` long flag)\n     - Add differential test cases for R2.2 (SIGINT suppression)\n     - Add differential test cases for R2.3 (combined `-ai` flags)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/tee ./cmd/tee/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/tee/ -count=1` to verify all tests pass (AC2)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/tee/` to verify no issues (AC3)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (SRD, main.go, tee_test.go) and was about to begin implementation. I had identified what changes are needed but had not yet written any code. The implementation plan is:\n   \n   **main.go changes:**\n   - Change `parseFlags` signature to `func parseFlags(args []string) (bool, bool, []string)` returning `(appendMode, ignoreInterrupts, files)`\n   - Add long flag handling for `--append` and `--ignore-interrupts` in the flag parsing loop\n   - In `main()`, after `parseFlags`, if `ignoreInterrupts` is true, call `signal.Ignore(os.Interrupt)` (need to import `os/signal`)\n   - Update the `main()` function to destructure the new return value\n   \n   **tee_test.go changes:**\n   - Add differential tests for multi-file + append combined\n   - Add test for `--append` long flag\n   - Add test for `-i` SIGINT suppression\n   - Add test for combined `-ai` flags\n   - Add test for `--ignore-interrupts` long flag\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the complete modified `cmd/tee/main.go` implementing SIGINT suppression (R2.2), long flag support for `--append` (R2.1) and `--ignore-interrupts` (R2.2), and ensuring R2.3 (combined flags) works. Then write the updated `cmd/t